NAME
    coretop - hardware and telemetry dashboard of the loaded core

SYNOPSIS
    coretop [-w] [--once [--json]]

DESCRIPTION
    With no options, 'coretop' requires a real interactive terminal to drive an
    auto-refreshing dashboard and therefore refuses over buffered module
    output after verifying that a session is attached.

    With --once, 'coretop' prints a single non-interactive snapshot combining
    the attached session's info, summary, telemetry counters, sprite/palette/
    audio summaries, and EmuSen process resource usage, then exits.

OPTIONS
    -w
        Request a separate frontend window. Currently fails with
        "coretop: -w is not supported by this frontend."

    --once
        Print a single-frame snapshot and exit without an interactive TTY.

    --json
        Emit the --once snapshot as compact JSON (requires --once).

EXAMPLES
    coretop --once
    coretop --once --json
    coretop
    coretop -w

EXIT STATUS
    0   Snapshot printed (--once).
    1   No session attached, interactive TTY unavailable, or unsupported flag.

SEE ALSO
    sysinfo(1), summary(1), regs(1), sprites(1), channels(1), pal(1),
    counters(1), profile(1)
